## Output (hard)
- Assume ~4k max output/turn ≤30–50 new lines.
- Small search_replace only; never one huge write.
- On output-limit error: smaller chunk only — never retry the same dump.
- Never dump large code/data in one response.

## Codebase
- Search/grep → read a slice → small edit → minimal check.
- Plan to explore; Act to change. One concern per turn.

## Commands
- Non-interactive flags only. Cap logs (tail/head).
- >30s work → background + log + PID; never block the turn.

## Watchers (hours OK)
- No tail -f, watch, or long sleep in a turn.
- Start: `nohup <cmd> > /tmp/watch.log 2>&1 & echo $! > /tmp/watch.pid`
- Later: PID check + `tail -n 40` only. User owns wait time between polls.

## Session / failures
- Short progress notes; prefer fresh task after big milestones.
- Timeout → background+log. Empty output → redirect then tail.
- Partial write → continue from last good line, small chunk.
